-- title:
--   Cones are invariant under positive scaling
-- statement:
--   Let $E$ be a real inner product space, let $v \in E$ be a unit vector, and let $\vartheta$ satisfy $0 < \vartheta \le \pi/2$. Write
--   $$\tilde V(v,\vartheta) \;=\; \{\,h \ne 0 : \langle v,h\rangle/\|h\| > \cos\vartheta\,\}$$
--   for the cone with axis $v$ and apex angle $\vartheta$. If $h \in \tilde V(v,\vartheta)$ and $t > 0$, then
--   $$t\,h \;\in\; \tilde V(v,\vartheta).$$
--
--   This is the positive homogeneity of cones: membership depends only on the direction of $h$, not on its length, so the cone is a union of open rays from the origin. It is the property that makes cone conditions scale-invariant and hence compatible with the homogeneous singular weights $\|x-y\|^{-d-\alpha}$ appearing throughout.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The normalisations $\|v\| = 1$ and $0 < \vartheta \le \pi/2$ are the standing conventions of the definition of a double cone and are carried here for uniformity with the surrounding development.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/dbenbenn/quadratic-forms-sobolev/blob/7a1a680db2124d46ce370c91fd450aa454edf491/QuadraticFormsSobolev/ConeGap.lean#L256-L261

